Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.20 Cheats screen, page 2: Money (DW3_CHEATS builds only)

The Money row of the Cheats screen (port/options/cheats.c, docs/PORT_OPTIONS.md
"Cheats") adds +10000 or +100000 to GAME.money, or sets MONEY_MAX. The field
applies it at its first idle frame (openFieldMenu: no menu, no event, no fade),
the moment the field menu may open, because at the title the game's state is
not there yet (a new game or a load overwrites it). dw3_cheats_take_money
answers 0 while the master switch is off or the row is not armed, and uses
the one-shot up. Logs "dw3: P6.20 cheat money A -> B".

Every line is inside #ifdef DW3_CHEATS (CMake option DW3_CHEATS, default ON):
a build with -DDW3_CHEATS=OFF compiles field.c exactly as without this patch.

--- a/src/field/field_mode/field.c
+++ b/src/field/field_mode/field.c
@@ -13,6 +13,9 @@
 #include "overlay_host.h"
 char *getenv(const char *name);
 long strtol(const char *nptr, char **endptr, int base);
+#ifdef DW3_CHEATS
+#include "port_cheats.h"
+#endif
 #endif
 
 /* Has the battle's files read while the transition plays */
@@ -483,6 +486,18 @@
 static inline void openFieldMenu(FieldTask *task, FieldChildren *children) {
     if (FIELDSTG_state.menuOpen != 1 && FIELDSTG_state.busy == 0 && FIELDSTG_state.acting == 0) {
         do {
+#ifdef DW3_CHEATS
+            /* P6.20 Money (Cheats screen, page 2): the first idle frame of the
+               field adds the armed amount, or sets MAX; used up and logged */
+            {
+                s32 cheatMoney;
+
+                if (dw3_cheats_take_money(GAME.money, MONEY_MAX, &cheatMoney)) {
+                    fprintf(stderr, "dw3: P6.20 cheat money %d -> %d\n", (int)GAME.money, (int)cheatMoney);
+                    GAME.money = cheatMoney;
+                }
+            }
+#endif
 #if PORT_HOST
             {
                 const char *force = getenv("DW3_FORCE_MENU");
